WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.733
Your receptionist is
helping a patient.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:02.733
The phone rings.

00:00:02.733 --> 00:00:03.933
Later, the practice closes.

00:00:04.233 --> 00:00:04.967
Someone else calls.

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:08.100
Your team can’t be in
two places at once.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.167
But the caller still
needs a next step.

00:00:11.633 --> 00:00:14.500
FlowAudit builds AI
phone agents that support

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.000
staff through agreed workflows.

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:18.767
You agree which calls
and appointments it

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:19.233
handles,

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.100
and when a person steps in.

00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:23.400
Here’s a recorded
new-patient enquiry.

00:00:24.033 --> 00:00:24.500
Hiya.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.800
I just wanted to ring
in and book an

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:26.033
appointment.

00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:29.800
Thanks.

00:00:30.233 --> 00:00:32.100
Can you please tell me
if this is for you or

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:32.700
someone else?

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:33.833
It's for me.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:35.000
I'm a new in the area.

00:00:35.333 --> 00:00:37.167
I want to, you know,
register with the dentist

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.700
and then get checked up as well.

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:42.100
Got it.

00:00:42.233 --> 00:00:43.633
Are you looking for
a new patient check-up

00:00:43.633 --> 00:00:43.967
appointment?

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.700
The first available appointment
this afternoon

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:49.000
is at 2:30 or three
in the afternoon

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.267
or 3:30.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.800
Which one works for you?

00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:53.167
Can we do three o’clock?

00:00:53.633 --> 00:00:55.400
And here’s the booking
in Google Calendar.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:57.967
Your new patient
check-up appointment

00:00:57.967 --> 00:00:59.300
is booked for Wednesday,

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:00.767
the 7th of October

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:02.233
at three in the afternoon.

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:04.933
A clear next step for the caller.

00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:07.233
Support for your team
when the desk is busy,

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.700
or the practice is closed.

00:01:09.633 --> 00:01:11.900
We assess your scheduling,
phone forwarding and

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:13.100
patient-data requirements.

00:01:13.533 --> 00:01:15.700
Then configure and test
the agreed workflow with

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:16.133
your team.

00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:18.333
Activation follows your approval.

00:01:19.333 --> 00:01:21.800
Book a fifteen-minute
demo and fit assessment.

00:01:22.233 --> 00:01:24.100
Bring the person who
approves the purchase.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:26.533
We’ll look at your call
workflows and see

00:01:26.533 --> 00:01:27.767
whether FlowAudit fits.
